From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:54:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: apple: Start the J604 T8132 host as the J713 does

3949e3640d ("arm64: apple: enable qualified J713 SuperSpeed host
support") publishes the initial host role before the core initializes
and sets the CIO block up before xHCI starts, for the J713 only
(dwc3_apple_host_before_core_init()). That is the host start its
SuperSpeed qualification ran with, on its USB2-only port as well.

The J604 is the same SoC and, with the board change after this, runs
SuperSpeed on its ATC1 port. Give it the same host start on all three
ports, as the J713 has on both of its ports, instead of a third
sequence that no board has run with SuperSpeed.

This changes the host start of the J604's two USB2-only ports too; the
device test covers each port (USB2 device on ports 1 and 4, USB3 device
on port 2).

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
index f0e8008d65..f8f9220d3b 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
@@ -216,10 +216,17 @@ static void dwc3_apple_set_ptrcap(struct dwc3_apple *appledwc, u32 mode)
 	dwc3_set_prtcap(&appledwc->dwc, mode, false);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The T8132 host start qualified with SuperSpeed: the initial host role is
+ * published before the core initializes and the CIO block is set up before
+ * xHCI starts. J713 first; the J604 runs the same sequence on all its ports.
+ */
 static bool dwc3_apple_host_before_core_init(struct dwc3_apple *appledwc,
 					     enum dwc3_apple_state state)
 {
-	return state == DWC3_APPLE_HOST && of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713") &&
+	return state == DWC3_APPLE_HOST &&
+		(of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713") ||
+		 of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j604")) &&
 		of_device_is_compatible(appledwc->dev->of_node, "apple,t8132-dwc3");
 }
 
